Z||000023||GT Bastard||01-29-2001||08:13 AM||||I've been to Colorado a few times and I thought it was allright... I'm not a real big fan of Denver.  Hmmmmmmmm...||||reg||1
Z||000024||87ECO5||01-29-2001||08:28 AM||||Well, I wouldn't feel right about adding a vote for Ohio because ... I WANT TO GET THE HECK OUT OF HERE!!!!!  BORING!<P>I'm thinking Colorado, Wyoming or Montana.||||reg||1
Z||000025||ChadMan||01-29-2001||08:46 AM||||How about Phoenix/Scottsdale, AZ?  Scottsdale has a rapidly growing IT community.  Plus, Phoenix gets more than 300 days of sun every year.  It gets hotter than hell in the summertime, but you can escape it by driving 2 hrs north to Flagstaff, where it's 20 degrees cooler due to the elevation there.  And you're only 6 hrs from San Diego and the beach.||||reg||1
Z||000026||1FST2M6||01-29-2001||09:05 AM||||Atlanta is nice!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> we'll have a bigger house and more spare rooms soon.. <P>nudge nudge...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000027||WampusCat||01-29-2001||12:39 PM||||[QUOTE]Originally posted by My7Fieros:<BR>[B]Not here, thats for sure. Memphis is a sespool of filth and crime. <BR>Well...I wouldn't go that far.  I kinda like midtown.  Lots of cool stuff in walking distance. Nice little resturants, bars, park, zoo, etc.  I does get damn near unbearable hot and muggy here in summer. I lived in Yuma, AZ for a few years and it was MUCH more comfortable there in summer than here.  It's also table flat for miles around here.  The nearest hill or curvy road is like a hundred miles away.  IT jobs?  Maybe you could learn blues harmonica or how to make barbeque instead.  Guess another non-vote for Memphis.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
