Z||000037||beer_stud_21||01-30-2001||11:39 PM||||Hawaii is alright if you like to smoke pot and go to the beach.  Of which I don't do either very often.  I've lived here on the big island for 10 yrs.  Its boring as **** .  If you need an IT job you would have to go to Honolulu on Oahu.  The other drawback is it would cost you about $800 bucks to ship your Fiero over here from the west coast.  Well, gotta go.....  I followed a black GT fastback home from town today.  The sound that thing made... GAWD!!  I think I've come down with this Fiero feaver thing I hear everyone talking about.  I sure as hell hope I can get this 85 GT im looking at.  I gotta get my fiero-fix soon, or i might die!<P>-Marlin aka: stupidhaole in hawaiian  ;-) ||||reg||1
Z||000038||Coconut||01-31-2001||03:25 PM||||Beer_stud_21, LOL!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>THAT is one of the things I miss most of all about living there! (J/K <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">) <BR>I can remember alot of those "good 'ol Kona Daze" before reality bit me in the A$# and said it was time to grow up. Funny thing about going back to visit when we went on our honeymoon, most of my cousins were still stuck in that same rut, so in a way....I'm glad I left and got the heck off island. Only problem is my wife wouldn't mind living there if she didn't have to move so far away from her family. I basically told her the same thing you just mentioned, but she fell in love with the place. I wouldn't mind going back, but only for a couple years max, that's it.<P>Cruisin'  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">,<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Coconut's_Signature_1.JPG"> ||||reg||12
